OL,3,CGovernment should ease energy policy
OL,4,Ccosts for 'concerned' businesses, says
OL,5,CE.On
OL,7,FThe boss of E.On UK has called on the
OL,8,FGovernment to ease pressure from
OL,9,Fenergy policy costs on business
OL,10,Felectricity bills to help "concerned"
OL,11,FUK firms.
OL,13,FChris Norbury, the chief executive of
OL,14,Fthe UK energy firm, said shifting
OL,15,Fpolicy cost into general taxation
OL,16,Fwould help spark further investment
OL,17,Ffrom businesses and help support the
OL,18,Ftransition to renewables.
OL,26,@rD@[OUrD@eO]
