OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1786411079
OL,3,CGovernment should ease energy policy
OL,4,Ccosts for 'concerned' businesses, says
OL,5,CE.On
OL,7,FHe said: "Whether it's small, medium
OL,8,For big businesses, they are concerned
OL,9,Fabout rising energy costs, some of the
OL,10,Frising commodity costs and therefore
OL,11,Fdon't want to see an impact from
OL,12,Fhigher policy costs."
OL,14,FE.On has suggested that the Government
OL,15,Fcould seek to shift policy costs, such
OL,16,Fas the renewable obligation and feed-
OL,17,Fin tariffs from electricity bills into
OL,18,Fgeneral taxation, or a dedicated
OL,19,Fenergy transition fund to help firms.
OL,26,@oD@JOUtD@UO]
